 236:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c **** /*
 237:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   Assign the draw color for all drawing functions.
 238:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   color may be 0 or 1. The actual color is defined by the display.
 239:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   With color = 1 the drawing function will set the display memory to 1.
 240:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   For OLEDs this ususally means, that the pixel is enabled and the LED 
 241:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   at the pixel is turned on.
 242:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   On an LCD it usually means that the LCD segment of the pixel is enabled, 
 243:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   which absorbs the light.
 244:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   For eInk/ePaper it means black ink.
 245:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c **** 
 246:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   7 Jan 2017: Allow color value 2 for XOR operation.
 247:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c ****   
 248:BSP/u8g2/u8g2_hvline.c **** */
